abstract: "Balazi, Allaire, Jolivet and Omnes (2025) asked whether a fourth-order moment-based nonconforming Stokes element on tetrahedra can be obtained by adding fifteen quintics to the quartics. It cannot: an alternating face functional vanishes on all quintics and equals 1/34650 on the Vandermonde sextic, which repairs the element (proof). For face moments of degree n and cell moments of degree n-1 the kernel on P_(n+2) is seven-dimensional for every n, degree n+2 misses (n-1)(n-2)/2 directions and degree n+3 is necessary and sufficient for n>=3 (proof). Minimal symmetric enrichments exist for every n (proof); triangles never need extra degree; a numerical Stokes test shows rates consistent with fourth order. Unrefereed candidate. Original code is MIT-licensed; see LICENSES.md."
